  "title": "Fix the misconfigured account",
  "estimatedMinutes": 20,
  "instructions": "## The audit found everything\n\nA previous administrator set up the student records system in a hurry. The **Security scanner** shows the result: a public bucket, databases and SSH open to the world, an all-powerful user with no MFA and two long-lived keys.\n\n## Do this\n\nWork through the findings until the scanner shows **no high or medium findings**:\n\n- make the `student-records` bucket private and encrypted;\n- close port 22 and the database port 3306 to the internet in `db-sg` and `web-sg` (SSH only from `10.0.0.0/16`; 3306 only from `web-sg`, written as `sg:<its id>`);\n- make `records-db` private, encrypted and backed up (7 days);\n- give user `kofi` MFA, at most one access key, and replace the administrator policy with the `records-operator` policy.\n\nDo not delete the resources: the system must keep working.",
  "config": {
    "panels": [
      "resources",
      "network",
      "iam",
      "scanner"
    ]
  },
  "initialState": {
    "seq": 8,
    "resources": [
      {
        "id": "sg-0001",
        "type": "sg",
        "name": "web-sg",
        "rules": [
          {
            "port": 80,
            "protocol": "tcp",
            "source": "0.0.0.0/0"
          },
          {
            "port": 22,
            "protocol": "tcp",
            "source": "0.0.0.0/0"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "sg-0002",
        "type": "sg",
        "name": "db-sg",
        "rules": [
          {
            "port": 3306,
            "protocol": "tcp",
            "source": "0.0.0.0/0"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "i-0003",
        "type": "vm",
        "name": "records-web",
        "region": "af-west-1",
        "zone": "a",
        "size": "small",
        "image": "Ubuntu 24.04",
